error[ffi_parameter_type]: `p` of `va_scrub` is declared `counted_by`, and `fixedbugs-2103-variadic.h` gives `va_scrub` 1 parameter and then `...`, where `p` stands — C counts in what its pointer points at, and there the pointer has no type, so no count can be held to what is lent
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2103-a-counted-lend-past-a-variadic-prototype-is-told-on-the-binding.hero:21:31
     |
  21 |     function va_scrub(k: i32, p: ptr counted_by 4 lent) -> i64  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |                               ^
  note: spec § 13: a counted lend hands C `N` elements of the program's own, `N` the sibling that tells C how many. C11 6.5.2.2p7: past a prototype's `...` a call converts nothing, and `va_scrub` reads the pointer as the type its `va_arg` names, so nothing says what C counts in, and none of them can be held to a count
  note: write a header of your own that includes `fixedbugs-2103-variadic.h` and defines a `static inline` function of a new name with a fixed prototype, taking `p` as a pointer to the type `va_scrub` counts in and calling `va_scrub` with it; bind that function instead, and its prototype holds the unit the count is in; where `va_scrub` reads a format, write the format inside that function as a literal, and clang reads each conversion against the argument it is given

